Interfacial Phenomena — John W. M. Bush, MIT 18.357 (@fd-bush: 0, is #reference, #part-of @fd-sources) { r_1NGF93FPCCP3FKJS0RAMN929VN
John W. M. Bush. MIT 18.357 Interfacial Phenomena, Fall 2010, graduate. [All lecture notes and nineteen topic entries](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/18-357-interfacial-phenomena-fall-2010/pages/lecture-notes/) · [Projects](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/18-357-interfacial-phenomena-fall-2010/pages/projects/).

Study the full available notes and a substantial project. They develop surface tension, wetting, stress conditions, capillary rise, Marangoni flow, jets, sheets, instability, contact lines, spreading and waves. Return to whole derivations when an industrial coating, cleaning or small-fluid problem uses one of these effects.

The archive supplies a combined PDF and individual topic notes, not a claimed complete examination or lecture-video collection. MIT OCW's CC BY-NC-SA terms have component exceptions. Images, notes and project readings remain external sources.

**Return:** [Fluid dynamics sources — books, courses, methods and physical evidence](../Sources.lingua#r_3Y3TVV9VQAB50M2ZSECK5JTYVG).
